title: Repentance and Assurance – Godly Sorrow, Confession, and the Believer Kept by God
description: An overview of the teaching on repentance and assurance: repentance as a change of mind, godly sorrow, confession, the chastening of sons, and the believer kept by God.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-assurance.html

# An overview of the whole of studies/data/topics/assurance.json, drawing from every theme.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed but not reworded.

=== Introduction
# from the topic summary
--- Repentance and Assurance [title]
overline: Doctrine · Assurance
heading: Repentance and Assurance
sub: Godly sorrow, confession, and the believer kept by God.
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the study. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 13277, 15099
--- That ye may know
big: 1 John 5:13 | mark: that ye may know that ye have eternal life
lead: God Who cannot lie promised before the foundation of the world that whosoever believes on Christ Jesus, calling upon His name for salvation, has eternal life, and are sealed and regenerated by the Spirit that you may KNOW you are a child of God.
note: Eternal security. Once saved, always saved.

=== Repentance
# from 14979, 2293, 11437
--- Repent: a change of mind
big: Matthew 3:2
lead: Repent means to change your mind, to accept new information as true and have a change of heart, a conversion.
panel-warn: Not this | He is not saying "get your life together and stop sinning, the Kingdom of Heaven is here."
panel: But this | Repenting in relation to salvation is turning from a false belief in something to justify us before God, or turning from unbelief to believing His word.

# from 11437, 2293
--- Turning from sin follows
p: That discernment, if the new man created at salvation is fed, leads to a change in attitude towards sin. It becomes less desirable. The lusts of the flesh can lose their appeal.
p: If that new man isn't fed, and they continue walking in the flesh, they are still saved by the knowledge of the truth, but that discernment is dulled and God may have to chasten the person to work godly sorrow in their heart.
callout: Only faith in the risen Christ and belief in the promise of God that Jesus is the sole propitiation for all sin can save us.

=== Godly sorrow
# from 17858
--- Godly sorrow and the sorrow of the world
big: 2 Corinthians 7:10
panel-warn: Cain | The burden Cain couldn't bear was the punishment, but he sorrowed not unto repentance. He never changed his mind about what he had done.
panel: David | David's sorrow is godly, he cannot bear his own iniquity and hates his sin that brought him low, rather than resenting the punishment he'd received.

# from 5457, 5458
--- The work of sorrow
lead: This sincere sorrow for sin is not itself repentance, but rather, repentance is the work of that sorrow.
scripture: 2 Corinthians 7:11 | mark: carefulness; clearing of yourselves; indignation; fear; vehement desire; zeal; revenge
p: This is a helpful list, both for those of us seeking to get right with God regarding sin in our life, and how we should act, and for judging rightly the sincerity, be it godly or earthly sorrow, of those who have wronged us.
note: As many receive it in tears, many still receive the truth in joy.

=== Confession and forgiveness
# from 1677, 18021
--- If we confess our sins
big: 1 John 1:9
p: First John, the epistle, is written to the saved. Here the Bible tells us if we the saved, want fellowship with God and one another, to walk with God, to confess our sins to Him, and be forgiven them all by Christ, washed clean in His blood.
callout: This promise shows not only the faithfulness of God to forgive, but also that our sin in the flesh is not held against our ledger in Heaven.

# from 18022
--- Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation
big: Psalm 51:12
p: David is not writing that he is afraid to lose his salvation, but seeking the confidence in it again that has been marred by his transgressions and the fear from the chastening he has received.
center: God wants to forgive us more than we want to be forgiven.

# from 7252, 1728
--- Not earned by penance
panel-warn: Perfect contrition | It requires the sinner to be 100% honest, 100% contrite, about 100% of their sins, that depends on the sinner alone, not the blood of Christ.
panel: Grace | We confess our sins to God knowing He's forgiven them already, that we have eternal grace that's never lost or taken away, in Christ Jesus.
p: Penance isn't how we earn forgiveness. Forgiveness is given by grace and mercy. Working to maintain God's grace makes grace no more grace. [[Romans 11:6]] [[Isaiah 1:18]]

# from 8698
--- New every morning
big: Lamentations 3:22-23
p: No matter how backslidden. No matter how snared in sin. No matter how the devil accuses you before God, in Christ Jesus you are forgiven.
callout: For a saved believer who has been sealed by the Spirit, it is never too late to turn back to God and away from your sins. Like the Prodigal son, returning to the Father.

=== Chastened as sons
# from 4826, 13935
--- Whom the Lord loveth he chasteneth
big: Hebrews 12:6
p: We are punished here on earth for our sins. Sometimes very harshly. Sometimes with death.
p: And so God punished David, yet He put away David's sin, because he had the imputed righteousness of Jesus Christ. His faith in God's word.
refs: 2 Samuel 12:13-14; Luke 12:48

# from 2535, 14971
--- Chastened, yet saved
panel: Ananias and Sapphira | Their being in Heaven when they die, justified by faith and Jesus' imputed righteousness didn't keep them from sinning, nor did it stop God from punishing them with their lives.
panel: Delivered unto Satan | God allows Satan to destroy us in the flesh. The hope in church discipline is that the person gets right. But if not, at least in death they are free from the sin and present with the Lord.
p: We saved are held to a higher standard than the unsaved, and we are punished here in this earth, sometimes more so than the unsaved, who are not God's children. [[Acts 5:1-5]] [[1 Corinthians 5:5]]

=== Kept by God
# from 1718, 12335
--- None shall pluck them out
big: John 10:28-29 | mark: they shall never perish
p: Once you are saved you are always saved, always His, always His sheep.
callout: Once saved always saved is not just a slogan, it is the truth of the Gospel and the crux of the Gospel, without which you cannot claim to have faith.

# from 4581, 10835, 13942
--- Sealed unto the day of redemption
big: Ephesians 4:30
p: Once we believe we are sealed by the Holy Spirit as the earnest, the down payment as it were, until redemption, where God makes good on His promise, on the day of the Lord.
p: We who are saved know that we have the Holy Spirit testifying within us that we are the sons of God.

# from 15541, 15618, 1560, 5571
--- Answering the errors
panel-warn: Falling away | If someone chooses atheism after having full knowledge of salvation, they were never saved. They believed in vain.
panel-warn: Enduring to the end | Too many false teachers assert that perseverance is for our spiritual salvation. It is for grace and protection during tribulation and persecution.
panel-warn: Judas | Not only wasn't Judas saved, he was a reprobate and Jesus knew this.
panel: The answer | Salvation cannot be lost, only refused.

=== Summary
# from 14979, 5457, 1677, 8698, 4826, 1718, 4581
--- Summary
point: Repentance | Repent means to change your mind, to accept new information as true and have a change of heart.
point: Godly sorrow | Sincere sorrow for sin is not itself repentance, but rather, repentance is the work of that sorrow.
point: Confession | If we are honest we confess our sins, and they are forgiven already in Christ.
point: Mercy | It is never too late to turn back to God and away from your sins.
point: Chastening | We are punished here on earth for our sins, yet He put away David's sin.
point: Kept | Once you are saved you are always saved, always His, always His sheep.
point: Sealed | We are sealed by the Holy Spirit as the earnest until redemption.

